# jemdoc: fwtitle

# = *Zhengzhong Jin*

~~~
 {}{img_left}{./photo1.jpg}{}{320}{}{}
*Research Interest:* I have a broad interest in cryptography and related topics in theoretical computer science. 
# I'm working on Succinct Non-interactive ARGuments (SNARGs), zero-knowledge protocols, and secure multi-party computation.

# My research focuses on the foundations of cryptographic proof systems. In particular, I'm interested in building cryptographic proofs with the following ``magical'' features: 
#- *Succinctness:* Generating /very short/ proofs for verifying long and complicated computations, and 
#- *Zero-Knowledge:* Proving the truth of a statement without revealing why the statement is true.

#My work has built the first succinct non-interactive cryptographic proofs for /any deterministic computation/ from standard assumptions, and the first non-interactive zero-knowledge cryptographic proofs for NP from Diffie-Hellman assumptions. Both results resolve long-standing open problems in cryptography. My research draws various techniques from complexity theory, mathematical logic, and numerical analysis.

# I am also exploring the intersection between cryptographic proof systems and other important topics in theoretical computer science, such as mathematical logic and machine learning.

I am an assistant professor at the [https://www.khoury.northeastern.edu/ Khoury College of Computer Science] at [https://www.northeastern.edu/ Northeastern University]. I am a member of the 
[https://neucrypt.github.io/ Cryptography and Privacy Group], the [https://www2.ccs.neu.edu/theory/ Theory Group], and the [https://cyber.northeastern.edu/ Cybersecurity and Privacy Institute]. Previously, I received my Ph.D. from Johns Hopkins University, where I was fortunately co-advised by [https://www.cs.jhu.edu/~abhishek/ Abhishek Jain] and [https://www.cs.jhu.edu/~lixints/ Xin Li]. After that I was a postdoctoral associate at [https://www.csail.mit.edu/ MIT CSAIL], mentored by [https://people.csail.mit.edu/vinodv/ Vinod Vaikuntanathan].  
I received my bachelor's degree from Mathematics Department at Fudan University, and was advised by Yunlei Zhao.

*Program Committee:* CRYPTO 2024, 2025, TCC 2023, 2024, 2025, PKC 2024, Asiacrypt 2025.

/*Contact:*/ zh.jin (AT) northeastern (DOT) edu, albusmath at gmail dot com.
